error[B0223]: this call can throw, and it is not marked with `try`
 --> check/try_covers_right.bloom:5:43
  |
5 | public func bad(_ a: Int) throws -> Int { g(a) + (try h(a)) }
  |                                           ^^^^ a throwing call
  |
help: write `try` before it (`try?` for `none` on an error, `do { try … } catch { … }` to handle it)
  = docs: https://github.com/OxyHQ/Bloom/blob/main/docs/bloom-lang-spec.mdx#6-expressions-and-control-flow

warning[B0225]: `??` never falls back: the `try?` covers it, and this is `Int`
 --> check/try_covers_right.bloom:6:44
  |
6 | public func never(_ a: Int) -> Int? { try? g(a) ?? h(a) }
  |                                            ^^^^ never `none`
  |
help: for the fallback of the `try?`, write `(try? g(a)) ?? …`
  = docs: https://github.com/OxyHQ/Bloom/blob/main/docs/bloom-lang-spec.mdx#62-control-flow-and-errors-20
